      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The Depot Theatre, opened in 1979, still performs in Westport’s historic Amtrak station, blending art with railroad heritage.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Westport%2C_New_York",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Westport hosts Camp Dudley, the nation’s oldest continuously operating summer camp, founded in 1885 by Sumner F. Smith.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Westport%2C_New_York",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Across from downtown, the Westport Library, completed in 1888, sits on a sloping lawn that becomes a green oasis.",
